ected Wednesday afternoon through Thursday\nevening producing periods of heavy rainfall and potential flash\nflooding.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-09-18T00:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Northwestern San Juan Mountains; Southwest San Juan Mountains; Four Corners/Upper Dolores River; Animas River Basin; San Juan River Basin","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.328d48753250deb934179a81042cd35b327b1d36.003.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.328d48753250deb934179a81042cd35b327b1d36.003.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-09-16T05:37:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 160537 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 1137 PM MDT Tue Sep 15 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Flash flooding will be possible as potentially record moisture passes through western Colorado and eastern Utah. - Flood Watch in effect for SE Utah and SW Colorado Wednesday through Thursday. - While vulnerable locations like slot canyons and burn scars ","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-09-16T06:44:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Subtropical moisture streaming into the area will continue to feed shower and thunderstorm activity through the week. These storms will bring a threat of heavy rainfall and the potential for excess runoff...especially over recent burn scars. Widespread wetting rainfall is expected over the next several days which will eliminate the threat of critical fire weather. ...GUSTY ERRATIC WI","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":{"station_id":"ctz01","station_name":"Cortez","distance_km":5.4,"soil_temp_5cm_f":63.9,"soil_temp_15cm_f":64.92,"soil_moisture_5cm":null,"soil_moisture_15cm":null,"precip_in":null,"eto_in":null,"vapor_pressure":null,"solar_radiation":0,"wind_speed_mph":2.5,"air_temp_f":62.19,"relative_humidity